<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20959] FLR-ECRO: fsync() of unmodified EC file blocks on unavailable OST</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20959</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;fsync()&lt;/tt&gt; of an EC file that was not modified (e.g. opened read-only, or RDONLY layout with no dirty pages) blocks until an unavailable data OST returns, because &lt;tt&gt;cl_sync_file_range()&lt;/tt&gt; sends OST_SYNC to every stripe.  See the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20212" title="FLR-ECRO: verify non-write RPCs do not block client " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20212"&gt;LU-20212&lt;/a&gt; test results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;osc_io_fsync_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; lov_io_end_wrapper &amp;lt; lov_io_fsync_end &amp;lt; cl_io_end &amp;lt; cl_io_loop &amp;lt; cl_sync_file_range &amp;lt; ll_fsync &amp;lt; vfs_fsync_range &amp;lt; do_fsync
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same happens from writeback (&lt;tt&gt;ll_writepages()-&amp;gt;cl_sync_file_range()&lt;/tt&gt; in the flush worker).  A stripe with no dirty or uncommitted pages on this client has nothing to sync, so the OST_SYNC for it could be skipped, making &lt;tt&gt;fsync()&lt;/tt&gt; of an unmodified file a no-op that does not depend on OST availability.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
